[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3579541361","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113173#issuecomment-3579541361","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113173","id":3579541361,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VW3dx","user":{"login":"unova-01","id":65930619,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTMwNjE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65930619?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01","html_url":"https://github.com/unova-01","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T06:43:46Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T06:43:46Z","body":"The reason this happens is because that code only works on an Autoload. The documentation does mention that, but only as a code comment above the code snippet demonstrating how to do an ``await`` with ``scene_changed``. Perhaps the warning that it only works on an Autoload should be made more explicit, but you can get this to work as intended very easily. Simply move the contents of your ``_on_button_pressed()`` function to an Autoloaded script, then call that function from the button press, and it will produce the desired output.\n\nI've made a very quick change to the MRP to demonstrate this, and it should now work as intended.\n\n[test-modified.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23763335/test-modified.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3579541361/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3580351272","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113173#issuecomment-3580351272","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113173","id":3580351272,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VZ9Mo","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T09:15:18Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T09:15:18Z","body":"I'd say this is clearly documented, both in the signal and the method:\n> The current scene node is immediately removed from the tree. From that point, `Node.get_tree()` called on the current (outgoing) scene will return null. `current_scene` will be `null`, too, because the new scene is not available yet.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3580351272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3581136091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113173#issuecomment-3581136091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113173","id":3581136091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Vc8zb","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T12:37:12Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T12:37:12Z","body":"Note that  `get_tree()` returning `null` is not the only potential issue with the example from the MRP. As mentioned in the docs, the scene being changed will be freed from the memory \"at the end of the frame\":\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/9dd6c4dbac70b28e8156255c3a2b78722772b036/doc/classes/SceneTree.xml#L59\n\nThis means that if the method awaiting `scene_changed` signal \"is within the scene being changed\" then such method will never be resumed after await because the \"awaiting object\" will be freed before the `scene_changed` signal is emitted.\n\nSo e.g. this will not throw an error (as `get_tree()` result is stored before exiting the tree) but also it will not print anything (the `Main` node to which this script is attached in the MRP is freed before the `scene_changed` signal emission):\n```gdscript\nextends Control\n\nfunc _on_button_pressed() -> void:\n\tvar scene_tree := get_tree()\n\tscene_tree.change_scene_to_packed(preload(\"res://scene.tscn\"))\n\tawait scene_tree.scene_changed\n\tprint_debug(scene_tree.current_scene.get_path())\n```\n\n---\n\n> The reason this happens is because that code only works on an Autoload.\n\nThis is not true though. Using an autoload is a possible solution, but anything ensuring the awaiting object is not freed before the signal emission would work. E.g. this works just fine in the MRP (static function is not being called on the instance which gets freed on the scene change):\n\n``` gdscript\nextends Control\n\nfunc _on_button_pressed() -> void:\n\tchange_scene(get_tree())\n\nstatic func change_scene(scene_tree: SceneTree) -> void:\n\tscene_tree.change_scene_to_packed(preload(\"res://scene.tscn\"))\n\tawait scene_tree.scene_changed\n\tprint_debug(scene_tree.current_scene.get_path())\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3581136091/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583203304","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113173#issuecomment-3583203304","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113173","id":3583203304,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Vk1fo","user":{"login":"heppocogne","id":83043568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMDQzNTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83043568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne","html_url":"https://github.com/heppocogne","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heppocogne/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T21:00:56Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T21:00:56Z","body":"@unova-01 @AThousandShips @kleonc \nThank you!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583203304/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583632746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113173#issuecomment-3583632746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113173","id":3583632746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VmeVq","user":{"login":"unova-01","id":65930619,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTMwNjE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65930619?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01","html_url":"https://github.com/unova-01","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/unova-01/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T00:25:48Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T00:25:48Z","body":"> This is not true though. Using an autoload is a possible solution, but anything ensuring the awaiting object is not freed before the signal emission would work.\n\nGood to know, thanks! In hindsight it was a bit hasty to say it only works with an autoload.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583632746/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]